    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00127',',AA.Den00127,Ed-U-Games tm,20060708,10,ThUn,ScAs,,ScFa,cassini prob;cassini;saturn;astronomy,,aPRA1_65 zPRA1_30,,,,,Science/Astronomy/Solar System,When did the Cassini probe enter into orbit around Saturn?,,Answer=20040701,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00128',',AA.Den00128,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,6,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,declaration;independence;declaration of independence,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Declaration of Independence Declared?,Twelve colonies voted in favor of the Declaration of Independence. New York abstained. This Declaration stated that the colonies were free and independent states; absolved of all allegiance to England. It made official what had already been happening; as the War of Independence was in full swing.,Answer=17760704,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00129',',AA.Den00129,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;new york;battle of new york;ny,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of New York?,The New York and New Jersey campaign was a series of engagements in the American Revolutionary War between forces led by General Sir William Howe; the British commander-in-chief; and the army under General George Washington; the American commander-in-chief. Beginning with the landing on Staten Island on July 3; 1776; British forces gained control of New York City and drove the Americans across New Jersey and into Pennsylvania.,Answer=17760703,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00130',',AA.Den00130,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,siege;boston;siege of boston ended,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Siege of Boston ended?,The Siege of Boston (April 19; 1775 – March 17; 1776) was the opening phase of the active American Revolutionary War; in which the Continental Army surrounded the city of Boston; Massachusetts; to prevent movement by the British Army within.,Answer=17760317,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00131',',AA.Den00131,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;princeton;battle of princeton;nj,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Princeton?,Howe sent troops south to take on Washington in Trenton. The American troops sidestepped the British forces in Trenton; instead battling them in Princeton. The Battle of Princeton fought on Jan 3; 1776 was won by the Americans at the last moment; forcing the British to withdraw to New Brunswick,Answer=17760103,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00132',',AA.Den00132,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,canada,,aPRA1_80 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Colonial Attack on Canada?,In September 1775 Arnold set off with an American force to capture Quebec. It was not until December 31 that Arnold~s troops were ready to attack. The attack failed and the Americans were repulsed after suffering heavy losses.,Answer=17751231,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00133',',AA.Den00133,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,us navy,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the U.S. Navy Created?,On November 28; the Continental Congress authorized the establishment of the American Navy. Although the Navy was to play only a minor role in the war; the success of American privateers in interrupting British trade was an important factor aiding the patriot cause.,Answer=17751128,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00134',',AA.Den00134,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,king george;rebellion,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When did King George Declares Colonies in Rebellion?,On 23 August 1775 King George III of Great Britain declared; "The colonies are in open and avowed rebellion. The die is now cast. The colonies must either submit or triumph.",Answer=17750823,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00135',',AA.Den00135,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;battle of bunker hill;ma;battle of bunker hill;ma,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Bunker Hill?,The Americans occupied Bunker Hill overlooking Boston on the evening of June 16th. The British; commanded by General Gage; had no choice but to attack the Americans. On the afternoon of the 17th; Gage~s forces attacked. In a hard fought battle; the American were forced to withdraw. While the British were victorious; they suffered heavy losses.,Answer=17750616,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00136',',AA.Den00136,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;ticonderoga;battle of ticonderoga i;ny,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Ticonderoga I?,The capture of Fort Ticonderoga was an event early in the American Revolutionary War. On May 10; 1775; Colonels Ethan Allen and Benedict Arnold surprised and captured the small British garrison at Fort Ticonderoga. Cannons captured at the fort were subsequently hauled away and used to fortify Dorchester Heights and break the stalemate at the siege of Boston,Answer=17750510,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00137',',AA.Den00137,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;concord;battle of concord;ma,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Concord?,Forewarned by Paul Revere; American militiamen fought 800 British troops on April 19th; 1775. The battle broke out at Concord. Seventy-three British soldiers were killed and over 200 were wounded. The Americans lost 49 soldiers and suffered 39 wounded.,Answer=17750419,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00138',',AA.Den00138,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;saratoga;battle of saratoga;ny,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Saratoga?,The British withdrew to Saratoga; where they were surrounded by American troops. The British had no choice but to surrender which they did on October 13; 1777. One quarter of the British forces in North America thus surrendered; and; while many battles were yet to be fought; American Independence was assured.,Answer=17771013,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00139',',AA.Den00139,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;germantown;pa;battle of germantown;pa,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Germantown?,After Howe had occupied Philadelphia; Washington attacked British troops at Germantown. The Americans planned a four pronged attack. The morning was foggy; and American coordination broke down. As a result; the attack failed; and the American troops were forced to withdraw.,Answer=17770922,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00140',',AA.Den00140,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;brandywine;battle of brandywine;pa,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Brandywine?,At the end of August; General Howe brought his army south by sea; threatening Philadephia. On September 10th; Howe~s forces attacked the American troops blocking his way to Philadelphia at Brandywine. In a day long battle; the British vanquished the American forces. The Americans; however; were able to extract their army.,Answer=17770910,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00141',',AA.Den00141,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;bennington;battle of bennington;vt,,aPRA1_160 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Bennington?,The Battle of Bennington was a battle of the American Revolutionary War; taking place on August 16; 1777; not at its namesake of Bennington; Vermont; but instead a few miles over the border in Walloomsac; New York. An American force of 2;000 New Hampshire and Massachusetts militiamen; led by General John Stark with aid from Colonel Seth Warner; defeated a combined force of 1;250 Brunswick mercenaries; Canadians; Loyalists; and Native Americans led by Lieutenant Colonel Friedrich Baum.,Answer=17770816,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00142',',AA.Den00142,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;orinsky;battle of orinsky;ny,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Orinsky?,An American relief force sent to relieve the siege of Fort Schuyler was ambushed by British and Native Americans at Orinsky. The Americans managed to fight themselves out of the ambush; severly depleting the British forces and opening the way for the later relief of the fort.,Answer=17770806,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00143',',AA.Den00143,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,massacre;jane mccrea;massacre of jane mccrea,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Massacre of Jane McCrea?,On 27 July 1777; Jane McCrea; who was engaged to a British officer was killed and scalped by native Americans.,Answer=17770727,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00144',',AA.Den00144,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;ticonderoga;battle of ticonderoga ii,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Ticonderoga II?,The British captured Fort Ticonderoga on July 6; 1777. They accomplished this task painlessly by stationing cannons on a peak overlooking the fort. The Americans then withdrew to fight another day.,Answer=17770706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00145',',AA.Den00145,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;trenton;battle of trenton;nj,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Trenton?,On December 26th; Washington~s Army crossed the Delaware and surprised the British at Trenton. The main attack was made by 2;400 troops under Washington on the Hessian Garrison. Washington~s troops acheived total surprise and defeated the British forces.,Answer=17761226,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00146',',AA.Den00146,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,washington;retreat,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was Washington~s Retreat Through N.J.?,The British captured Fort Washington on Northern Manhattan Island on November 16; 1776; without much difficulty. Washington proceeded into New Jersey. He was pursued by Howe all the way south until he successfully crossed the Delaware River.,Answer=17761116,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00147',',AA.Den00147,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;valcour bay;battle of valcour bay;ny,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Valcour Bay?,On the 11th of October; Sir Guy Carleton~s squadron approached; and there ensued the first battle fought between an American and a British fleet.,Answer=17761011,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00148',',AA.Den00148,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,benedict arnold;traitor,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was Benedict Arnold declared a Traitor?,In an act that has made his name synonymous with treason in American history; General Benedict Arnold conspired to turn his command of West Point over to the British. In return; he was to receive money and become a general in the British army.,Answer=17800925,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00149',',AA.Den00149,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;camden;battle of camden;nj,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Camden?,In July 1780; Horatio Gates was at Camden; commanding a force of 1;400 Continentals. He was soon joined by patriot troops from Virginia and North Carolina. General Cornwalis was also in Camden; with an army of 3;000. Gates and Corwalis soon found themselves facing each other across a field. The two sides advanced on each other; with the British regulars opposite the Carolina militia men. After a few minutes; the Carolina line gave way. This led to a general crumbling of the American lines; and the American army was soon in complete retreat.,Answer=17800715,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00150',',AA.Den00150,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,siege;charleston;siege of charleston,,aPRA1_90 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Siege of Charleston ended?,The British began a southern strategy by beginning a seige of Charleston. The siege lasted until May 9th when British artillery fire was close enough to set the town on fire and force a surrender.,Answer=17800509,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00151',',AA.Den00151,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,bonne homme richard;serapis,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the sea battle between the Bonne Homme Richard and HMS Serapis?,The most remarkable single ship duel of the American Revolution was between the Bonne Homme Richard commanded by John Paul Jones and the HMS Serapis. The duel took place on September 23; 1779. The Serapis was a 50 gun ship that outgunned the Bonne Homme Richard which was barely sea worthy. When the captain of the Serapis hailed the Bonne Homme Richard and demanded surrender; John Paul Jones answered:" Surrender be dammed; I have not begun to fight." The Bon Homme Richard went on the vanquish the Serapis.,Answer=17790923,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00152',',AA.Den00152,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,stonypoint,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When did the Americans recapture Stony Point?,In their first northward action since the surrender at Saratoga; the British captured the American fort at Stony Point. Under the direction of General Washington; the Americans recaptured the fort; suffering only minimal casualties.,Answer=17790715,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00153',',AA.Den00153,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;monmouth;battle of monmouth;nj,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Monmouth?,The Battle of Monmouth was an American Revolutionary War battle fought in New Jersey on June 28; 1778; that was a turning point of the American Revolution. The main Continental Army under George Washington attacked the rear of the British Army~s column led by Sir Henry Clinton as they left Monmouth Court House.,Answer=17780628,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00154',',AA.Den00154,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,settlers;massacr;wyoming,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Settler~s Massacred at Wyoming?,At the end of June 1778; a group of 900 Tories and Native Americans struck the Wyoming Valley of Pennsylvania. A small force of militia and 60 regulars under the command of Colonel Zebulon Butler attacked the attackers and was butchered. All of those not killed on the battlefield were later tortured to death.,Answer=17780625,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00155',',AA.Den00155,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,treaty;amity;france,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Treaty of Amity with France declared?,After the American victory at Saratoga; the French were ready to enter into an agreement with the Americans. On January 7; 1778; the French royal council declared unanimously in favor of a treaty of amity and commerce with the United States. It was followed on February 6th with a treaty of alliance.,Answer=17780107,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00156',',AA.Den00156,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,valley forge;encampment,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Valley Forge Winter Encampment started?,With the British Army secure in Philadelphia; the American army settled into winter quarters at Valley Forge. It was a winter of hardship and suffering for the troops. It was also a winter of training; in which the American troops were taught how to be professional soldiers.,Answer=17771231,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00157',',AA.Den00157,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,treaty;paris;treaty of paris,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Treaty of Paris?,On September 3; 1783; a peace treaty was formally signed between Great Britain and the United States. This treaty officially ended the Revolutionary War.,Answer=17830903,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00158',',AA.Den00158,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,10,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;battle of yorktown;va;battle of yorktown;va,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Yorktown?,The Siege of Yorktown was a victory by a combined assault of French Forces led by General Comte de Rochambeau and American Forces led by General George Washington; over a British Army commanded by General Lord Cornwallis. The surrender of Cornwallis~s army caused the British government to negotiate an end to the American Revolutionary War.,Answer=17811019,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00159',',AA.Den00159,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;eutaw springs;battle of eutaw springs;sc,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Eutaw Springs?,The final battle of 1781 took place at Eutaw Springs when General Greene~s Army approached the army of Colonel Stewart located in Eutaw Springs 30 miles northwest of Charleston.,Answer=17810908,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00160',',AA.Den00160,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;battle of hobkirks hill;nc;battle of hobkirks hill;nc,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Hobkirks Hill?,On April 25; 1781; Greene placed his men on Hobkirk~s Hill; a pine-covered ridge running east and west a mile north of Camden; North Carolina. Lord Rowden attacked the American position; and some of the Continental soldiers broke and ran; thus destroying the integrity of the American defensive line. Although the Battle of the Hobkirk~s Hill was a tactical British victory; Rowden was forced to withdraw.,Answer=17810425,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00161',',AA.Den00161,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;guilford court house;battle of guilford court house;nc,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Guilford Court House?,American forces under the command of General Greene attacked British forces commanded by General Cornwalis at Guilford Court House. The British forces won a tactical victory; but British losses were too heavy for Cornwalis~ forces to bear.,Answer=17810315,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00162',',AA.Den00162,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,articles;confederation;ratified;articles of confederation,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Articles of Confederation Ratified?,With the approval of Maryland; the Articles of Confederation took effect. The Articles stated that there was a perpetual union between the states; while individual states remained sovereign. The states retained every right not given to the central government.,Answer=17810301,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00163',',AA.Den00163,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;cowpens;battle of cowpens;sc,,aPRA1_95 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of Cowpens?,American General Morgan defeated a British force of regulars under the command of Colonel Tarleton. Morgan~s troops enveloped the British in a classic military action that captured all of the British forces.,Answer=17810117,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00164',',AA.Den00164,Ed-U-Games tm,20070501,12,EvPoMi EvWaAm EvWaBa,Hi18 HiUS HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,HiMaBa,battle;king mountain;battle of king mountain;nc,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was the Battle of King Mountain?,On October 7; 1780 the militia arrived at the base of the mountain and surrounded it. Soon they began scaling it on all sides. The patriots had the advantage that the slopes of the mountain were very wooded; while the summit was not; exposing the Tory troops to attack by the concealed Americans. The defenders~ losses quickly mounted and; when Ferguson was killed; the fight went out of the remaining soldiers. Of the Tory troops; 157 were killed; 163 were severely wounded and 698 were captured. The patriot militia lost only 28 killed and 62 wounded.,Answer=17801007,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
