    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00371',',AA.Den00371,Ed-U-Games tm,20070601,10,EvWaAm,Hi16 HiNoNoUS,NoNoUS,CiUS HiWa,mad anthony wayne;green springs farm;va;battle of green springs farm;battle,,aPRA1_85 zPRA1_30,,,,,History/American/Military Action/Revolutionary War,When was Mad Anthony Wayne repulsed at Green Springs Farm; VA?,,Answer=17810706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00372',',AA.Den00372,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;battle;hubbardton,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Hubbardton?,General St Clair’s troops left Fort Ticonderoga on 6th July 1777 hastening to put as much ground between themselves and the pursuing army of General Burgoyne in their retreat to the South.  After 26 miles the Americans reached Hubbardton where the battle took place.  The Americans did not think the British could catch up with then that fast and were caught by surprise.  The fighting was intense and Major Grant was killed.  The British won the battle.,Answer=17770706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00373',',AA.Den00373,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;washington;commission;resign commission,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did George Washington resign his commission?,On 23 December 1783 - Following a triumphant journey from New York to Annapolis; George Washington; victorious commander in chief of the American Revolutionary Army; appears before Congress and voluntarily resigns his commission; an event unprecedented in history.,Answer=17831223,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00374',',AA.Den00374,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;washington;farewell address,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did George Washington deliver his farewell address to his army?,November 2; 1783 - George Washington delivers his farewell address to his army. The next day; remaining troops are discharged.,Answer=17831102,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00375',',AA.Den00375,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;treaty;paris;ratified;congress,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was The Treaty of Paris ratified by Congress?,Congress ratify the treaty on January 14; 1784.  It was signed by the United States and Great Britain on 3 September 1783.,Answer=17840114,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00376',',AA.Den00376,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;great britain;treaty;paris,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was The Treaty of Paris signed by the United States and Great Britain?,September 3; 1783 - The Treaty of Paris is signed by the United States and Great Britain. Congress will ratify the treaty on January 14; 1784.,Answer=17830903,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00377',',AA.Den00377,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;congress;end,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Congress officially declare an end to the Revolutionary War?,April 11; 1783 - Congress officially declares an end to the Revolutionary War.,Answer=17830411,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00378',',AA.Den00378,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;england;hostilities;declare,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did England officially declare an end to hostilities in America?,February 4; 1783 - England officially declares an end to hostilities in America.,Answer=17830204,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00379',',AA.Den00379,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;charleston;south carolina,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British evacuate Charleston; South Carolina?,December 14; 1782 - The British evacuate Charleston; South Carolina.,Answer=17821214,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00380',',AA.Den00380,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;peace treaty;paris,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the preliminary peace treaty signed in Paris?,November 30; 1782 - A preliminary peace treaty is signed in Paris. Terms include recognition of American independence and the boundaries of the United States; along with British withdrawal from America.,Answer=17821130,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00381',',AA.Den00381,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;congress;great seal;united states,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Congress adopt the Great Seal of the United States of America?,On 20 June 20 1782 - Congress adopts the Great Seal of the United States of America.,Answer=17820620,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00382',',AA.Den00382,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british;surrendered;yorktown;clinton,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British Army surrender at Yorktown?,On 19 October 1781 - As their band plays the tune; "The world turned upside down;" the British army marches out in formation and surrenders at Yorktown. Hopes for a British victory in the war against America are dashed. In the English Parliament; there will soon be calls to bring this long costly war to an end.,Answer=17811019,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00383',',AA.Den00383,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;cornwallis;truce flag;yorktown;washington,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did General Cornwallis raise the flag of truce at Yorktown?,on 17 October 1781 - As Yorktown is about to be taken; the British send out a flag of truce. General Washington and General Cornwallis then work out terms of surrender.,Answer=17811017,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00384',',AA.Den00384,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;yorktown;cornwallis;siege,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the siege of Yorktown begin?,29 September 1781 - General Washington; with a combined Allied army of 17;000 men; begins the siege of Yorktown. French cannons bombard General Cornwallis and his 9000 men day and night while the Allied lines slowly advance and encircle them.,Answer=17810928,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00385',',AA.Den00385,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;new london;connecticut;benedict arnold;arnold;loot;connecticut,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,Benedict Arnold; as a British general; burn the port of New London; Connecticut.  When did this happen?,September 6; 1781 - Benedict Arnold~s troops loot and burn the port of New London; Connecticut.,Answer=17810906,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00386',',AA.Den00386,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;french fleet;british fleet;yorktown;naval battle;de grasse;thomas;chesapeake;blockade,,aPRA1_145 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the French fleet defeat the British fleet just off the City of Yorktown?,On 5 September 1781 - Off Yorktown; a major naval battle between the French fleet of de Grasse and the outnumbered British fleet of Adm. Thomas Graves results in a victory for de Grasse. The British fleet retreats to New York for reinforcements; leaving the French fleet in control of the Chesapeake. The French fleet establishes a blockade; cutting Cornwallis off from any retreat by sea. French naval reinforcements then arrive from Newport.,Answer=17810905,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00387',',AA.Den00387,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;yorktown;cornwallis;french fleet;british fleet,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did General Cornwallis arrive in Yorktown?,On 1 August 1781 - After several months of chasing General Greene~s army without much success; General Cornwallis and his 10;000 tired soldiers arrive to seek rest at the small port of Yorktown; Virginia; on the Chesapeake Bay.,Answer=17810801,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00388',',AA.Den00388,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;guilford courthouse;battle;cornwallis;carolinas,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the battle of Guilford Courthouse?,March 15; 1781 - Forces under General Cornwallis suffer heavy losses in the Battle of Guilford Courthouse in North Carolina. As a result; Cornwallis abandons plans to conquer the Carolinas and retreats to Wilmington; then begins a campaign to conquer Virginia with an army of 7500 men.,Answer=17810315,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00389',',AA.Den00389,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;cowpens;south carolina;american victory;morgan;tarleton,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the American victory at Cowpens; South Carolina?,January 17; 1781 - An American victory at Cowpens; South Carolina; as General Daniel Morgan defeats British General Tarleton.,Answer=17810117,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00390',',AA.Den00390,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;arnold;benedict arnold;traitor;west point;tarrytown,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was Benedict Arnold discovered to be a traitor?,On 23 September 1780 - A British major in civilian clothing is captured near Tarrytown; New York. He is found to be carrying plans indicating Benedict Arnold intends to turn traitor and surrender West Point.  He had been aiding the British since May of 1779.,Answer=17800923,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00391',',AA.Den00391,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;american defeat;fishing creek;south carolina;gates;general gates;cornwallis,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Major American defeat at Fishing Creek; South Carolina?,On 16 August 1780 there was a big defeat for the Americans  at Fishing Creek; South Carolina as forces under General Gates are defeated by troops of General Charles Cornwallis; resulting in 900 Americans killed and 1000 captured.,Answer=17800816,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00392',',AA.Den00392,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british;evacuate;savannah;georgia,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British evacuate Savannah; Georgia?,On 11 June 11 1782 - The British evacuate Savannah; Georgia.,Answer=17820611,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00393',',AA.Den00393,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;house of commons,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the House of Commons votes against further war in America?,27 February 27 1782 - In England; the House of Commons votes against further war in America.,Answer=17820227,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00394',',AA.Den00394,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;yorktown;surrendered;reinforcement troops;reinforcements;chesapeake bay,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,The British surrendered Yorktown on 19 October 1781.  When did seven thousand reinforcement troops arrive to aid them?,On 24 October 1781 - 7000 British reinforcements under General Clinton arrive at Chesapeake Bay but turn back on hearing of the surrender at Yorktown.,Answer=17811024,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00395',',AA.Den00395,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;benedict arnold;arnold;west point;clinton;washington,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Benedict Arnold assume command of West Point?,August 3; 1780 - Benedict Arnold is appointed commander of West Point. Unknown to the Americans; he has been secretly collaborating with British General Clinton since May of 1779 by supplying information on General Washington~s tactics.,Answer=17800803,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00396',',AA.Den00396,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;french soldiers;newport;rhode island;blockaded;british fleet,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,Six thousand French soldiers arrive at Newport; Rhode Island to aid the American cause.  When did this happen?,July 11; 1780 - 6000 French soldiers under Count de Rochambeau arrive at Newport; Rhode Island. They will remain there for nearly a year; blockaded by the British fleet.,Answer=17800711,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00397',',AA.Den00397,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;springfield;battle;new jersey,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Springfield?,June 23; 1780 - American forces defeat the British in the Battle of Springfield; New Jersey.,Answer=17800623,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00398',',AA.Den00398,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;horatio gates;gates;southern army;congress,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was General Horatio Gates commissioned by Congress to command the Southern Army?,June 13; 1780 - General Horatio Gates is commissioned by Congress to command the Southern Army.,Answer=17800613,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00399',',AA.Den00399,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;massachusetts;born free;black slaves;constitution,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was a new Massachusetts constitution endorsed asserting ~all men are born free and equal;~ which includes black slaves?,June 11; 1780 - A new Massachusetts constitution is endorsed asserting "all men are born free and equal;" which includes black slaves.,Answer=17800611,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00400',',AA.Den00400,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british;charleston;garrison;american defeat,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British capture Charleston and its 5;400-man garrison?,May 12; 1780 - The worst American defeat of the Revolutionary War occurs as the British capture Charleston and its 5400-man garrison (the entire southern American Army) along with four ships and a military arsenal. British losses are only 225.,Answer=17800512,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00401',',AA.Den00401,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british;fort moultrie;charleston;south carolina;charleston harbor,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British capture Fort Moultrie at Charleston; South Carolina?,The British attack begins against Charleston as warships sail past the cannons of Fort Moultrie and enter Charleston harbor. Washington sends reinforcements.  On 6 May 1780 - The British capture Fort Moultrie at Charleston; South Carolina.,Answer=17800506,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00402',',AA.Den00402,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;adams;john adams;peace;england,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was John Adams appointed by Congress to negotiate peace with England?,September 27; 1779 - John Adams is appointed by Congress to negotiate peace with England.,Answer=17790927,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00403',',AA.Den00403,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;john paul jones;fight!;i have not yet begun to fight!;england;frigate,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did John Paul Jones make the famous statement  ~I have not yet begun to fight!~?,September 23; 1779 - Off the coast of England; John Paul Jones fights a desperate battle with a British frigate. When the British demand his surrender; Jones responds; "I have not yet begun to fight!" Jones then captures the frigate before his own ship sinks.,Answer=17790923,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00404',',AA.Den00404,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;loyalists;connecticut;fairfield;new haven harbor,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Loyalists raid coastal towns in Connecticut; burning Fairfield; Norwalk and ships in New Haven harbor?,July 5 11; 1779 - Loyalists raid coastal towns in Connecticut; burning Fairfield; Norwalk and ships in New Haven harbor.,Answer=17790705,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00405',',AA.Den00405,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;spain;declare war;england,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Spain declare war on England?,June 16; 1779 - Spain declares war on England; but does not make an alliance with the American revolutionary forces.,Answer=17790616,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00406',',AA.Den00406,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;norfolk;virginia;british troops;burn,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did British troops burn the cities of Portsmouth and Norfolk?,May 10; 1779 - British troops burn Portsmouth and Norfolk; Virginia.,Answer=17790510,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00407',',AA.Den00407,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;southern campaign;savannah;georgia;augusta,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the British begin their Southern Campaign with the capture of Savannah?,December 29; 1778 - The British begin a major southern campaign with the capture of Savannah; Georgia; followed a month later with the capture of Augusta.,Answer=17781229,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00408',',AA.Den00408,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;siege;newport;rhode island,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the siege against Newport; Rhode Island?,August 8; 1778 - American land forces and French ships attempt to conduct a combined siege against Newport; Rhode Island. But bad weather and delays of the land troops result in failure. The weather-damaged French fleet then sails to Boston for repairs.,Answer=17780808,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00409',',AA.Den00409,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;france;britain,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did France join in and declare war against Britain?,July 10; 1778 - France declares war against Britain.,Answer=17780710,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00410',',AA.Den00410,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;monmouth;battle;new jersey;washington;clinton;troops,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Monmouth?,27 June 1778 - The Battle of Monmouth occurs in New Jersey as Washington~s troops and General Clinton~s troops fight to a standoff.,Answer=17780627,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00411',',AA.Den00411,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british;henry clinton;clinton;howe,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did British General Henry Clinton replace General Howe as commander of all British forces in the American colonies?,May 8; 1778 - British General Henry Clinton replaces General Howe as commander of all British forces in the American colonies.,Answer=17780508,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00412',',AA.Den00412,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;british parliament;parliament;peace commission,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Peace Commission created by the British Parliament to negotiate with the Americans?,March 16; 1778 - A Peace Commission is created by the British Parliament to negotiate with the Americans. The commission then travels to Philadelphia where its offers granting all of the American demands; except independence; are rejected by Congress.,Answer=17780316,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00413',',AA.Den00413,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;steuben;baron von steuben;prussia;continental army;troops;desertion;harsh winter,,aPRA1_155 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Baron von Steuben of Prussia join the Continental Army?,February 23; 1778 - Baron von Steuben of Prussia arrives at Valley Forge to join the Continental Army. He then begins much needed training and drilling of Washington~s troops; now suffering from poor morale resulting from cold; hunger; disease; low supplies and desertions over the long; harsh winter.,Answer=17780223,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00414',',AA.Den00414,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;treatie;amity;commerce;alliance;paris;french;recognize;washington,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When were the Treaties of Amity & Commerce and Alliance signed in Paris?,February 6; 1778 - American and French representatives sign two treaties in Paris: a Treaty of Amity and Commerce and a Treaty of Alliance. France now officially recognizes the United States and will soon become the major supplier of military supplies to Washington~s army.,Answer=17780206,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00415',',AA.Den00415,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;valley forge;pennsylvania;continental army;washington;winter quarters,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the Continental Army set up winter quarters at Valley Forge?,On 17 December 1777 - At Valley Forge in Pennsylvania; the Continental Army led by Washington sets up winter quarters.,Answer=17771217,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00416',',AA.Den00416,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;congress;articles of confederation,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Congress adopt the Articles of Confederation making it the sole authority of the new national government?,On 15 November 1777 - Congress adopts the Articles of Confederation as the government of the new United States of America; pending ratification by the individual states. Under the Articles; Congress is the sole authority of the new national government.,Answer=17771115,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00417',',AA.Den00417,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;saratoga;battle;benedict arnold;arnold;general burgoyne;burgoyne;british;casualties,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Saratoga?,On 7 October 7 1777 - The Battle of Saratoga results in the first major American victory of the Revolutionary War as General Horatio Gates and General Benedict Arnold defeat General Burgoyne; inflicting 600 British casualties with American losses at 150.,Answer=17771007,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00418',',AA.Den00418,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;battle;bennington;militiamen;vermont;massachusetts;german hessians;burgoyne;general burgoyne,,aPRA1_145 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Bennington?,On 16 August  1777 -In the Battle of Bennington; militiamen from Vermont; aided by Massachusetts troops; wipe out a detachment of 800 German Hessians sent by General Burgoyne to seize horses.,Answer=17770816,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00419',',AA.Den00419,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;marquis de lafayette;lafayette;continental army;french;french aristocrat;washington,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the Marquis de Lafayette join the Continental Army?,On 27 July 27 1777 - Marquis de Lafayette; a 19 year old French aristocrat; arrives in Philadelphia and volunteers to serve without pay. Congress appoints him as a major general in the Continental Army. Lafayette will become one of General Washington~s most trusted aides.,Answer=17770727,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00420',',AA.Den00420,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;brandywine;brandywine creek;general washington;washington;battle,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Brandywine Creek?,On 9 September 9 1777 - In the Battle of Brandywine Creek; General Washington and the main American Army of 10;500 men are driven back toward Philadelphia by General Howe~s British troops. Both sides suffer heavy losses.,Answer=17770909,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00421',',AA.Den00421,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;general burgoyne;burgoyne;fort ticonderoga;british;lake champlain,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did General Burgoyne recapture Fort Ticonderoga for the British?,July 6; 1777 - General Burgoyne~s troops stun the Americans with the capture of Fort Ticonderoga on Lake Champlain. Its military supplies are greatly needed by Washington~s forces. The loss of the fort is a tremendous blow to American morale.,Answer=17770706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00422',',AA.Den00422,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;star and strips;congress;13 stars;13 stripes,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the ~Stars and Strips~ flag mandated by Congress?,June 14; 1777 - The flag of the United States consisting of 13 stars and 13 white and red stripes is mandated by Congress.,Answer=17770614,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00423',',AA.Den00423,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;battle;battle ridgefield;connecticut;benedict arnold;arnold;british defeat;ridgefield;connecticut,,aPRA1_140 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Ridgefield; Connecticut?,April 27; 1777 - American troops under Benedict Arnold defeat the British at Ridgefield; Connecticut.,Answer=17770427,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00424',',AA.Den00424,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;george washington;washington;delaware river;delaware;trenton;new jersey;washington;christmas;german mercenaries,,aPRA1_150 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did George Washington cross the Delaware River and capture Trenton New Jersey?,December 25 26; 1776 - On Christmas; George Washington takes 2400 of his men and recrosses the Delaware River. Washington then conducts a surprise raid on 1500 British-Hessians (German mercenaries) at Trenton; New Jersey.,Answer=17761225,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00425',',AA.Den00425,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;newport;rhode island;british;british,,aPRA1_125 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the naval base at Newport; Rhode Island; captured by the British?,December 6; 1776 - The naval base at Newport; Rhode Island; is captured by the British.,Answer=17761206,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00426',',AA.Den00426,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;san francisco;city;west coast;spanish missionaries,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,During the Revolutionary War; the City of San Francisco was established on the west coast?  When was this?,October 9; 1776 - San Francisco is established by Spanish missionaries on the California coast.,Answer=17761009,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00427',',AA.Den00427,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;jefferson;franklin;silas deane;treatie,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Congress appoints Jefferson; Franklin and Silas Deane to negotiate treaties with European governments?,September 26; 1776 - Congress appoints Jefferson; Franklin and Silas Deane to negotiate treaties with European governments. Franklin and Deane then travel to France seeking financial and military aid.,Answer=17760926,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00428',',AA.Den00428,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;nathan hale;hale;executed;spying;i only regret that i have but one life to lose for my country,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was Nathan Hale executed for spying?,September 22; 1776 - After he is caught spying on British troops on Long Island; Nathan Hale is executed without a trial; his last words; "I only regret that I have but one life to lose for my country.",Answer=17760926,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00429',',AA.Den00429,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;battle;long island;british;americans defeat,,aPRA1_135 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the Battle of Long Island?,August 27 29; 1776 - General Howe leads 15;000 soldiers against Washington~s army in the Battle of Long Island. Washington; outnumbered two to one; suffers a severe defeat as his army is outflanked and scatters. The Americans retreat to Brooklyn Heights; facing possible capture by the British or even total surrender.,Answer=17760827,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00430',',AA.Den00430,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;july 4;colonial delegation;lee~s resolution;jefferson;declaration;declaration of  independence;parchment,,aPRA1_155 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the actual signing of the Declaration of Independence?,On 28 June 1776; Jefferson~s Declaration of Independence is ready and is presented to the Congress; with changes made by Adams and Franklin. On July 2; twelve of thirteen colonial delegations (New York abstains) vote in support of Lee~s resolution for independence. On July 4; the Congress formally endorses Jefferson~s Declaration; with copies to be sent to all of the colonies. The actual signing of the document occurs on August 2; as most of the 55 members of Congress place their names on the parchment copy.,Answer=17760802,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00431',',AA.Den00431,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;continental congress;13 colonies,,aPRA1_105 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the Continental Congress authorizes each of the 13 colonies to form local governments?,May 10; 1776 - The Continental Congress authorizes each of the 13 colonies to form local governments.,Answer=17760510,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00432',',AA.Den00432,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;dorchester heights;boston;british;fort ticonderoga,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the American forces capture Dorchester Heights?,March 4 17; 1776 - American forces capture Dorchester Heights which overlooks Boston harbor. Captured British artillery from Fort Ticonderoga is placed on the heights to enforce the siege against the British in Boston. The British evacuate Boston and set sail for Halifax.,Answer=17760317,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00433',',AA.Den00433,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;king george iii;royal proclamation,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did King George III issue a royal proclamation closing the American colonies to all commerce and trade?,December 23; 1775 - King George III issues a royal proclamation closing the American colonies to all commerce and trade; to take effect in March of 1776. Also in December; Congress is informed that France may offer support in the war against Britain.,Answer=17751223,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00434',',AA.Den00434,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;thomas paine;common sense;pamphlet;best-seller,,aPRA1_130 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was Thomas Paine~s ~Common Sense~ published?,January 9; 1776 - Thomas Paine~s "Common Sense" is published in Philadelphia. The 50 page pamphlet is highly critical of King George III and attacks allegiance to Monarchy in principle while providing strong arguments for American independence. It becomes an instant best-seller in America. "We have it in our power to begin the world anew...American shall make a stand; not for herself alone; but for the world;" Paine states.,Answer=17760109,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00435',',AA.Den00435,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;naval engagement;valcour bay;lake champlain;gunship,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,In a major naval engagement of the war; the British defeated the Americans in the  Battle of Valcour Bay?  When did this happen?,October 11; 1776 - A big defeat for the inexperienced American Navy on Lake Champlain at the hands of a British fleet of 87 gunships. In the 7 hour Battle of Valcour Bay most of the American flotilla of 83 gunships is crippled with the remaining ships destroyed in a second engagement two days later.,Answer=17761011,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00436',',AA.Den00436,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;new hampshire;constitution;adopt,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,The first state to adopt a constitution was New Hampshire.  When did this happen?,January 5; 1776 - The assembly of New Hampshire adopts the first American state constitution.,Answer=17760105,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00437',',AA.Den00437,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;king louis xvi;france;munitions,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,The American revolutionaries needed foreign support and got it from King Louis XVI of France.  When did this happen?,May 2; 1776 - The American revolutionaries get the much needed foreign support they had been hoping for. King Louis XVI of France commits one million dollars in arms and munitions. Spain then also promises support.,Answer=17760502,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00438',',AA.Den00438,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;north carolina;continental congress;britain;independence,,aPRA1_115 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,The North Carolina assembly was the first to empower its delegates in the Continental Congress to vote for independence from Britain.  When was this?,April 12; 1776 - The North Carolina assembly is the first to empower its delegates in the Continental Congress to vote for independence from Britain.,Answer=17760412,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00439',',AA.Den00439,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;continental congress,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the Continental Congress state that Americans are ~resolved to die free men rather than live as slaves.~?,July 6; 1775 - The Continental Congress issues a Declaration on the Causes and Necessity of Taking Up Arms detailing the colonists~ reasons for fighting the British and states the Americans are "resolved to die free men rather than live as slaves.",Answer=17750706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00440',',AA.Den00440,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;american navy;congress;birthday,,aPRA1_110 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the American Navy established by Congress?,November 28; 1775 - The American Navy is established by Congress.,Answer=17751128,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00441',',AA.Den00441,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;continental congress,,aPRA1_100 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did the Continental Congress issues a Declaration on the ~Causes and Necessity of Taking Up Arms~?,July 6; 1775 - The Continental Congress issues a Declaration on the Causes and Necessity of Taking Up Arms detailing the colonists~ reasons for fighting the British and states the Americans are "resolved to die free men rather than live as slaves.",Answer=17750706,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00442',',AA.Den00442,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;first;post office;ben franklin;franklin;postmaster general,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When was the first American Post Office established with Ben Franklin as Postmaster General.,July 26; 1775 - An American Post Office is established with Ben Franklin as Postmaster General.,Answer=17750726,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00443',',AA.Den00443,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;battle;british;bunker hill;first;american troops;musket fire,,aPRA1_160 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,The first major battle between British and American troops was the Battle of Bunker Hill.  When was this?,On 17 June 1775 - The first major fight between British and American troops occurs at Boston in the Battle of Bunker Hill. American troops are dug in along the high ground of Breed~s Hill (the actual location) and are attacked by a frontal assault of over 2000 British soldiers who storm up the hill. The Americans are ordered not to fire until they can see "the whites of their eyes." As the British get within 15 paces; the Americans let loose a deadly volley of musket fire and halt the British advance. The British then regroup and attack 30 minutes later with the same result. A third attack; however; succeeds as the Americans run out of ammunition and are left only with bayonets and stones to defend themselves. The British succeed in taking the hill; but at a loss of half their force; over a thousand casualties; with the Americans losing about 400; including important colonial leader; General Joseph Warren.,Answer=17750510,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
    this.roundMap.set('AA.Den00444',',AA.Den00444,Ed-U-Games tm,20070807,10,EvWaAm LoHiBa LoPoCiHi,Hi18 HiNoNoUS Hi,NoNoUS,MiBa HiWa,american revolution;war;congress;washington;commander-in-chief;continental army;general washington,,aPRA1_120 zPRA1_30,,,,,Wars/US/American Revolution,When did Congress votes to appoint George Washington commander-in-chief of the Continental Army?,On 15 June 1775; the Congress unanimously votes to appoint George Washington general and commander-in-chief of the new Continental Army.,Answer=17750615,}P.AA.Pi.Th.Sy.Ta.DateLine-1.PD.gif');
